  "body": "I am writing a web worker script for a time-consuming job that keeps running while being able to be \"instantly\" adjusted by the main thread(Bunch of adjustment requests can frequently arrive to the worker thread from the main thread).\r\n\r\nSo in order to keep the job running and being able to be \"instantly\" adjusted, my web worker script has to be roughly like this:\r\n\r\n**Worker code**\r\n```\r\nlet lastTime = new Date().getTime();\r\nlet thisTime = lastTime;\r\n\r\nonmessage = (msg) =>\r\n{\r\n\twhile (...)\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t...\r\n\t\t...\r\n\t\t...\r\n\r\n\t\tthisTime = new Date().getTime();\r\n\t\tif (thisTime - lastTime > 100)\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tself.postMessage({askIfTheresAdjustment: true});\r\n\t\t\tlastTime = thisTime;\r\n\t\t\treturn;\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Main thread code**\r\n```\r\n...\r\n\r\nworker.addEventListener(\"message\", (msg) =>\r\n{\r\n\tif (msg.data.askIfTheresAdjustment)\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t// |unprocessedAdjustments| may be filled with adjustments at any time on the user's demand.\r\n\t\tworker.postMessage(unprocessedAdjustments);\r\n\t\tunprocessedAdjustments = {};\r\n\t}\r\n\t...\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe above code simulates *actively* getting messages, so that it is able to keep the time-consuming job running while being \"instantly\" adjusted from the main thread.\r\n\r\nHowever, the code has rather bad performance, because:\r\n\r\n1. thread switchings happen back and forth so frequently, thread switchings are so expensive;\r\n2. during a round trip of switchings, the web worker just bluntly blocks and waits without doing anything, leading to low concurrency.\r\n\r\nSo I would like to see a better feature that is efficient to *actively* get queued message, without having to rely on the passive onmessage method. I am hoping to hear from your thoughts on this issue.",
